\import{macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}

\taxon{Definition}
\title{Feedback operator}
\tag{ftip}
\tag{feedback}

\p{Let #{\mathcal F} be a declared signal space. A \strong{feedback operator}
is a possibly stochastic map}

##{
  F:\rho\longmapsto Z\in\mathcal F
}

\p{that uses only fields of the rollout record and separately declared
randomness. The signal #{Z} may contain a scalar reward, a preference,
step-level labels, a critique, or a structured verifier trace.}

\p{Section 2 of \citef{christiano2017deep} defines human-preference feedback.
Sections 3.2--3.4 of \citef{ouyang2022training} use demonstrations,
preferences, and a learned reward. \citef{lightman2023verify} distinguishes
process from outcome supervision. Section 2.2 of \citef{guo2025deepseek} uses
verifiable outcome feedback. The feedback operator is an FTIP synthesis of
these signal-producing mechanisms. Its output need not be scalar.}
